  {
    "number": 129,
    "title": "Add reversible Linux/WSL shared monitor setup and cutover",
    "body": "Refs #8.\n\nAdds reversible Linux/WSL shared-monitor setup to the hub package. Owners can inspect and review exact hook edits, apply one producer per source, and revoke its access before removing only unchanged owned entries. Private receipts retain recovery intent; unrelated hooks and trust settings survive. Codex Windows-to-WSL command construction is explicit and source-tested; actual client qualification remains separate.\n\nComposes Nanoleaf's owning preflight/shared/legacy CLI with the existing supervised state handoff. A fenced host can expose a running read projection for consumer readiness while refusing mutations. Activation verifies both consumers before opening admission. Owner moves revoke the old setup and create a fresh receipt against the destination. The current MCP delivery is preserved.\n\nValidation: Node 24 build/type checks; contract, lifecycle, state and MCP consumers/packages; host/setup, workflow and Linux isolated performance checks. Fourteen setup tests include stale edits, interrupted operations, edited/duplicate ownership, bounded input, private-field rejection, deadlines and competing credential claims. The offline hub archive is reproducible and passes installed tests. Real pinned Pixoo/Nanoleaf sources with disposable state pass credential revocation, both projections of an identified event, fenced handoff, legacy rollback and latest-state rollback. The Pixoo check also covers labels, notices, acknowledgment and renderer continuity. No personal installation, agent launch or physical writer ran.\n\nOpenSpec `gh-8-shared-monitor-installation` is synchronized and archived. Inventory after integrating #126: nine main specifications and eight archived changes. All previous CI jobs/suites remain; setup runs in both Python contract jobs.\n\nGuide: refreshed issue scope and shared-host narrative; updated the owner-migration sequence and source pins. Generation, five maintenance tests, browser/print checks and unchanged regeneration pass. Nine diagram deliveries pass 9/9 artifact checks. The migration viewer retains its documented vertical overflow; standalone first-screen containment is not claimed. Guide UI is exempt from human approval under docs/sdlc.md. Public publication is outside this request and remains pending; the served guide is older.\n\nIndependent Standards and Specification reviews and all five current-head CI jobs are required before guarded squash merge. Merged-main checks precede issue closure; newly confirmed source/tracker facts then need a guide follow-up. This PR does not auto-close the issue.\n",
    "state": "open",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/129",
